# H13 Chromium chain (D5 pass 13, one guarded call per stage, one heavy run at a time). The engine facts; the self-test of record
# (every witness whose cells or fixture paths H13 changed, whole: E-10 (the cured glide on slider, clipstale and the plate), E-11 (the
# readers, the new parts), E-13 (the lens travel's clockOf), E-3 (writeReach, checkToken on the hold)); every witness on the clean
# fixture; then the library builds on the new cells: cand12 (P-E13's baseline and the plant of every new member), C-A12's allkinds
# (the control on the mutation kinds and re-entry), HEAD (the changed witnesses' new cells); the glance stills; the CAP sheets
facts chromium
st-E-10 chromium
st-E-11 chromium
st-E-13 chromium
st-E-3 chromium
clean chromium
cand12-E-10 chromium --part hg13
cand12-E-11 chromium --part forms,tokens,census,reachin
plant-allkinds-E-10 chromium --part hg13 --hg13 kind,reentry
head-E-10 chromium --part hg13
head-E-11 chromium --part forms,tokens,census,reachin
glance-cand12 chromium
fxglance chromium
cap chromium
